A||||4||FieroMike||What cams?
Z||000000||FieroMike||05-27-99||09:20 AM||||Hello everyone! Just wondering what everyone would suggest as far as cams go.  I am getting the 3.1 rebuild from a local machine shop.  They offer a performance cam called Wolverine that will only cost $15.00 extra dollars bcz it is their brand.  To add Crane, or SpeedPro it will cost another $100 - $130 dollars.  Which one would be better? I don't remeber EXACTLY but the lift and duration is the same as the mild SpeedPro, it's not a huge duration and lift.
Z||000001||Eric||05-27-99||01:25 PM||||Fiero Mike, check out 3.1 build in the other forum.  I think I'm going to go with the GM performance cam Shaun recommended on that thread.  If you're looking for max horsepower, you're going to need an aggresive cam.  But $15 is cheap for a cam.  I would be sure to check out what other people who used it in their rebuilds think of the cam.  And be sure it's computer friendly.  It may be the case you will need to buy a name brand cam anyway, just to get the performance you want. 
Z||000002||GREENDANO||06-06-99||06:25 AM||||The GM performance cam works very well.  It comes with lifters too.  I have the big one in my 3.2  .427/.454 lift.  It pulls right from two grand to each shift.  (I have an auto)  With the big cam, a little gasket matching on the intake and a fresh overbore with a 3.1 Camaro crank, the 3.2 easily makes 190-200 HP.  Now all I have to do is save money ahead of time for the speading tickets...  :)
Z||000003||FieroMike||06-06-99||09:53 AM||||Greendano,<br>Thanks for the info!  I was wondering how well the car idles with the "big" cams?!  Is it really rough or not too bad?  Thanks!<br>-Mike
Z||000004||GREENDANO||06-07-99||08:55 PM||||Mike,<br> My GT Idles with a nice aggressive idle(for a V6)  It not quite my big block but it still has a mean growl.  You know it's not stock when it idles.<br>  Dan-O
